# Team Directory & User Profile — Feature Documentation

## Overview

This document describes the **Team Directory** enhancements and the new **User Profile** system that links team members to their post-meeting performance data.

---

## Features Added

### 1. Auto-Generated Login Key

When a new team member is created in the Team Directory, a **unique 10-character alphanumeric key** is automatically generated and stored.

- **Model field:** `TeamDirectory.key` (auto-generated on creation, read-only)
- **Purpose:** Used by team members to authenticate and view their personal dashboard
- **Uniqueness:** Each key is randomly generated and unique per user
- **Visible in:** Team Directory member cards (shown as 🔑 badge)

### 2. Send Email Button (✉ per user block)

Each team member card in the Team Directory has a **Send Credentials** button (envelope icon) that emails the member their login credentials.

- **Button location:** Action buttons area of each member card (purple envelope icon)
- **What it sends:** Name, Email, Slack ID, and Login Key
- **Backend endpoint:** `POST /api/team-directory/{id}/send-credentials/`
- **Condition:** Only appears if the member has an email address set

### 3. View Profile Button (👤 per user block)

Each team member card has a **View Profile** button (green person icon) that navigates to a detailed PUBG-inspired profile page.

- **Button location:** First button in the action buttons area (green icon)
- **Navigation:** Clicking navigates to `/team/{member_id}`
- **Frontend route:** `/team/:id` → `UserProfile.jsx`

### 4. User Profile Page (`/team/:id`)

A game-inspired profile dashboard showing:

| Section | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Hexagonal Avatar Banner** | Animated avatar with glowing rank badge (Bronze → Silver → Gold → Platinum → Diamond) |
| **Season Pass XP Bar** | Progress bar showing advancement from current rank to next rank |
| **K/D Style Stats** | Animated count-up numbers for Matches, Best Score, Worst Score, Rank, Words, Talk Time |
| **Info Cards** | Email, Slack ID, Employee Key, Join Date with icons |
| **Achievements** | 3D flip badges: First Blood, MVP, Clutch, Team Player, Legend |
| **Performance Radar** | 5-axis radar chart: Participation, Clarity, Sentiment, Relevance, Engagement |
| **Sparkline Trend** | Last 10 meetings score trend with 👑 crown on personal best |
| **Sentiment Timeline** | Area chart with gradient fill (red → gray → green), clickable points showing transcript snippets |
| **Recent Matches** | Game-history styled table with colored borders (green/amber/red) and hover animations |
| **Team Leaderboard** | Ranked list of all team members with scores and rank badges |
| **Streak Banner** | 🔥 animated banner if last 3 scores are improving |
| **Confetti** | Fires on page load if user is Diamond rank |
| **Sticky Float Card** | Bottom-right card showing rank emoji, name, score (collapses on mobile) |

### 5. Post-Meeting Score Computation

After every meeting completes, a Celery task automatically:

1. **Matches speakers to Team Directory** using fuzzy name matching:
   - Case-insensitive exact match
   - First-name only match
   - Bracket-stripped match (e.g., "John [slack:U123]" → "John")
   - Substring match
2. **Computes performance scores** from `SpeakerAnalysis` records
3. **Stores sentiment breakdowns** (positive/neutral/negative counts)
4. **Creates `UserMeetingScore` records** linked to both the team member and the meeting

**Celery task:** `compute_participant_scores` (runs 10 seconds after meeting completion)

---

## Data Flow

```
Meeting Ends
  └─→ process_meeting_pipeline (Celery)
        ├─→ Transcription + Summary + Action Items
        ├─→ distribute_action_items (5s delay)
        └─→ compute_participant_scores (10s delay)
              ├─→ Match speakers → TeamDirectory (fuzzy name matching)
              ├─→ Aggregate SpeakerAnalysis scores & sentiments
              └─→ Create/Update UserMeetingScore records
                    └─→ Data available on Profile Page graphs
```

---

## Database Model

### `UserMeetingScore`
| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `team_member` | FK → TeamDirectory | The matched team member |
| `meeting` | FK → Meeting | The meeting this score belongs to |
| `performance_score` | Float | Score 0-100 |
| `sentiment_positive` | Integer | Count of positive sentiment segments |
| `sentiment_neutral` | Integer | Count of neutral sentiment segments |
| `sentiment_negative` | Integer | Count of negative/concern sentiment segments |
| `contribution_summary` | Text | Summary of member's contribution |
| `word_count` | Integer | Total words spoken |
| `talk_time_seconds` | Integer | Total speaking time |
| `meeting_date` | DateTime | When the meeting occurred |

### `TeamDirectory.key`
| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `key` | CharField(10) | Auto-generated 10-character alphanumeric login key |

---

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `GET` | `/api/team-directory/` | List all team members |
| `POST` | `/api/team-directory/` | Create member (key auto-generated) |
| `PUT` | `/api/team-directory/{id}/` | Update member |
| `DELETE` | `/api/team-directory/{id}/` | Delete member |
| `POST` | `/api/team-directory/{id}/send-credentials/` | Email login credentials |
| `GET` | `/api/team-directory/{id}/profile/` | Full profile with scores, leaderboard, meeting history |

### Profile Response Shape
```json
{
  "member": { "id", "name", "email", "slack_id", "key", "created_at" },
  "overall_score": 72.5,
  "total_meetings": 12,
  "total_words": 4500,
  "total_talk_time": 1800,
  "best_score": 95.0,
  "worst_score": 42.0,
  "rank": 2,
  "leaderboard": [{ "id", "name", "score", "meetings" }],
  "meeting_history": [{
    "meeting_id", "meeting_title", "meeting_date",
    "performance_score", "sentiment_positive", "sentiment_neutral",
    "sentiment_negative", "word_count", "talk_time_seconds",
    "contribution_summary"
  }]
}
```

---

## Rank System

| Rank | Score Range | Badge |
|------|-----------|-------|
| Bronze | 0 – 30 | 🥉 |
| Silver | 31 – 50 | 🥈 |
| Gold | 51 – 70 | 🥇 |
| Platinum | 71 – 85 | 💎 |
| Diamond | 86 – 100 | 👑 |

## Achievement Badges

| Badge | Criteria |
|-------|----------|
| 🩸 First Blood | Attended first meeting |
| ⭐ MVP | Scored 90+ in any meeting |
| 🔥 Clutch | Score > 60 despite negative sentiment majority |
| 🤝 Team Player | 3+ meetings with positive sentiment majority |
| 👑 Legend | 10+ meetings with 80+ average score |

